1. **Outside safety audit at OpenAI:** METR and Redwood Research spent three weeks inside OpenAI. They found that 6ΓÇô25% of the activity from OpenAI's internal AI agents went unchecked by its monitoring system. They also found ways to hide actions from that system and to get out of Codex's sandbox. Marked normal, linked to the 22 Oct story.
2. **Study on coding-agent setups:** Researchers ran the same model inside Claude Code, OpenCode, and a minimal setup that only has a terminal. Claude Code and the minimal setup scored within 2 points of each other, but cost per task varied up to 3x. The choice of model mattered far more than the setup. Marked normal.

